{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Final rebar-debug report\n\nProblem\nA malformed or stale project criteria configuration caused plan review to return an unsigned INDETERMINATE result labeled as llm_unavailable, even though no provider call ran. This sent operators toward provider credentials instead of the installed-build/configuration mismatch.\n\nProven root cause\nThe assemble-criteria scripted step raised CriteriaError, but the generic workflow recorder preserved only an undifferentiated failed-step string. Gate dispatch therefore reached the source-blind degraded tail, which classified every unrecognized tail failure as an LLM outage. The loss of typed failure identity at the recorder boundary was the causal defect.\n\nExperiments\nA held-out end-to-end workflow test injected a sentinel CriteriaError at criteria assembly. Before the fix it reproduced the false llm_unavailable classification. The fix made it GREEN. Removing the structured dispatch route made the same test RED again, and restoring the route returned it to GREEN. The test also proves that non-CriteriaError failures retain generic LLM degradation behavior and that deterministic blockers/coverage survive the local config fault.\n\nFix\nCriteria assembly now emits a failed StepResult with stable failure_kind=criteria_config and the original diagnostic. Verdict dispatch recognizes only that exact failed assemble frame and marker before generic degradation, reruns the deterministic floor, preserves deterministic findings, reports config_fault without llm_unavailable, and gives actionable repository-checkout/installed-build remediation. The output schema documents the new structured fields.\n\nHeld-out disclosure\nThe original held-out source had been deleted and no byte-identical copy was available. The regression was reconstructed from the frozen behavioral contract before production edits; this limitation is disclosed rather than claiming source identity.\n\nValidation\nRED to GREEN to mutation RED to restored GREEN; 235 passed and 8 skipped in the focused validation; lint, typecheck, diff check, DCO, commit-ticket verification, and independent cross-review all passed. Gerrit change 1568 earned LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, zero unresolved comments, and merged on 2026-08-09.\n\nPer operator directive, this ticket remains in_progress and is not closed."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786306546341656001,"uuid":"9af40920-3603-448b-b644-53a6aee962e5"}